            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h2>

            <h3>What is the fastest way to check SIM owner details in Pakistan?</h3>
            <p>The fastest method is sending <strong>MNP to 667</strong> from the SIM you want to verify. Within 5–10 seconds, you receive the registered owner name and network operator.</p>

            <h3>How can I check all SIMs registered on my CNIC?</h3>
            <p>Send your <strong>13-digit CNIC number to 668</strong> without dashes. You will receive a message showing the total number of SIMs registered across all networks.</p>

            <h3>Is it legal to check SIM owner details online in Pakistan?</h3>
            <p>Yes, but only through <strong>official PTA methods</strong> like SMS to 668, MNP to 667, or official PTA portals. Unofficial databases violate digital privacy laws (PECA 2016).</p>
